  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">3. The Swedish International Biodiversity Programme (SwedBio) initierades 2002 vid Centrum f&#xF6;r Biologisk M&#xE5;ngfald (CBM), SLU. St&#xF6;det syftar till att st&#xF6;dja biodiversitet-fattigdomsfr&#xE5;gor genom kapacitetsuppbyggnad i Syd, integrering inom svensk utvecklingsfr&#xE5;gor samt int. dialog policyutveckling. st&#xF6;det SwedBio Bas &#xE4;r inriktat mot st&#xF6;d till verksamheten vid CBM och har en budget p&#xE5; tot 14 MSEK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Swedish International Biodiversity Programme (SwedBio) was initiated in 2002 at Centrum for Biologisk M&#xE5;ngfald (CBM), SLU. The aim is to more proactively address biodiversity-livelihoods concerns through capacity building in the South, integration of biodiversity aspects in Swedish dev. coop and int dialogue and policy dev. SwedBio core is focused on operations at CBM, with a total budget of 14 MSEK.</narrative>
  </description>
